---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import twygChop from '../assets/Logo_Chop.png';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<Image 
			src={twygChop} 
			alt="Twyg Logo Chop" 
			class="home-logo" 
		/>
		<main>
			<h1 class="title">John "Twyg" Hyde</h1>
			<p class="intro-body">
				John Hyde is an artist whose creative spirit is inspired by nature and emotion <br>
				evoked through the transformative powers of both the creation and <br>
				performance of his pieces.
			</p>
			<p class="intro-body">
				With a healthy respect for the level of emotion that can be felt while viewing unsettling pieces, he attempts to hone his work to help the viewer safely journey to a place where we can explore the darker side of ourselves. The creations are carefully crafted from traditional and innovative tools so that we can, through conscientious creation, and then sacred play, perhaps discover a path to knowing ourselves better.
			</p>
			<p class="intro-body">
				Are you here from the <a href="https://sca.org"  target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Society from Creative Anachronism?</a> Please see my SCA blog. While adjacent to my art practice, the SCA allows me to study historic art and use those influences in my own art practice.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
